---
term: Escalation
aka:
  - Recursive elevation
section: coordination
order: 20
definition: Raising a conflict or an [[externality]] to the parent or higher-order corporation whose charter covers every affected party.
seeAlso:
  - arbitration
  - parent-corporation
---
Escalation gives the Social Charter a recursive way to handle problems that are larger than any single corporation. Each step up reaches a charter with a broader common interest and a broader jurisdiction.

Escalation stops at the level whose jurisdiction matches the set of affected parties. Mancur Olson called that match the *principle of fiscal equivalence* (1969): the people who benefit from a public good, and only they, should decide on it and pay for it.
